.claude
# ── Generated at build time (ROADMAP §28.13/§28.14) ──────────────────────────
# ONE policy: anything `scripts/prebuild.ts` deterministically regenerates from
# committed sources is ignored, because CF regenerates all of it on every deploy
# (`wrangler.toml [build] command = "npm run build"` → npm's prebuild lifecycle
# hook). Tracking derived files only bought permanent diff churn — every dev run
# dirtied the tree. Two deliberate exceptions are called out at the bottom.
public/content-index.json
public/graph.json
public/albums.json
public/folders.json
public/slug-map.json
public/broken-links.json
public/image-dimensions.json
public/emotes/index.json
public/sitemap.xml
public/rss.xml
public/wiki-rss.xml
public/content/
# src/content/ is wiped (`rmSync`) and re-synced from content/ on every prebuild
# — see CLAUDE.md gotcha #1. It was tracked, which made 167 derived files look
# like source and invited edits that the next prebuild silently destroyed.
src/content/
#
# EXCEPTIONS — generated-looking but genuinely committed artifacts:
#  • public/music.json — NOT build-generated. Committed source of truth, written
#    by `npm run sync:music` (SoundCloud → R2). Prebuild only seeds `[]` if absent.
#  • public/og/*.png — MUST be committed. CF never sets PROCESS_OG, so og-gen
#    does not run on deploy; the cards ship as committed artifacts. This used to
#    be an ignore rule that 178 cards were force-added past, which meant any NEW
#    card was silently dropped and shipped as a missing OG image (ROADMAP §28.1).
#    `scripts/test-og.ts` now fails the build if a card is missing or untracked.

.dev.vars
.wrangler/
.playwright-mcp/
.music-sync-tmp/

# Automation / agent tooling output (not source)
daily-report.md
.codex/

# Local scratch / one-off debug scripts (not source)
scratch/
test-flexsearch.mjs

# Agent/audit output (root-level, not source)
anticipated-fails.md
audit-report.json
